  "notes": "Scaled so the skull is 120 mm wide (20 cm long) to sit on the forehead of a 58 cm head; the horns reach about 17 cm back over the head. The horns print separately: each one has a seat shaped exactly like the skull where it attaches, plus a 2 mm hole straight through the joint. Push a short piece of 1.75 mm filament into the hole as a pin, then glue (superglue or epoxy). Skull and horns: 3 walls, 10 % gyroid infill to keep them light. Spine pieces and arm pieces print flat side down; arm pieces are 59 × 42 mm. Ribs: 3 left + 3 mirrored right, scaled to 220 mm long to fit the printer. All plates use tree supports and a small brim.",
